'''booming<sup>1</sup>''' (bö′ming), ''p. a.'' [Ppr. of ''boom''<sup>1</sup>, ''v.''] Making a deep, hollow, continued sound (in any of the senses of the verb).
{{smaller block|<poem>All night the ''booming'' minute gun
Had pealed along the deep. ''Hemans'', The Wreck.</poem>
<poem>Still darker grows the spreading cloud
From which the ''booming'' thunders sound.</poem>
{{right|''Bryant'', Legend of the Delawares.}}}}
